<http://data.silknow.org/object/bc5499b8-2eba-3db4-b3cb-d154c3c9d733>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Loom width of woven silk, France, ca. 1717"@en , "Loom width of woven silk. The pattern consists of a symmetrical arrangement of fantastic flowers and fruit forms, and with the occasional spray or trail of flowers and leaves confined by bands of ribbon or lace ornament. Most of the design is woven in gold and silver threads, filé and frisé. Some details and outlines are in green silk which has faded at the front to pale blue. The ground is red silk damask with patterns of scallops and small sprays of flowers around the outlines of the main design, and fillings of spots within one space defined by a scrolling ribbon.\n\nWarps of white silk, binding pattern in 3/1 twill, and of red silk pattern warp in satin of 5.\nWefts of cream silk ground weft; green silk pattern weft; and gold and silver thread on silk core, filé and frisé, brocaded.\n\nThe selvedges are 0.25 inch green and white silk warp stripe, edged by 6 cords, 0.19 inch wide."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/9bc31733-5545-3dd0-b078-ad61660a3235> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/786d15dd-2448-351f-8da1-e7669a9f8b66> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Loom width of woven silk, France, ca. 1717"@en , "Loom width of woven silk. The pattern consists of a symmetrical arrangement of fantastic flowers and fruit forms, and with the occasional spray or trail of flowers and leaves confined by bands of ribbon or lace ornament. Most of the design is woven in gold and silver threads, filé and frisé. Some details and outlines are in green silk which has faded at the front to pale blue. The ground is red silk damask with patterns of scallops and small sprays of flowers around the outlines of the main design, and fillings of spots within one space defined by a scrolling ribbon.\n\nWarps of white silk, binding pattern in 3/1 twill, and of red silk pattern warp in satin of 5.\nWefts of cream silk ground weft; green silk pattern weft; and gold and silver thread on silk core, filé and frisé, brocaded.\n\nThe selvedges are 0.25 inch green and white silk warp stripe, edged by 6 cords, 0.19 inch wide."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/bc5499b8-2eba-3db4-b3cb-d154c3c9d733/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/bc5499b8-2eba-3db4-b3cb-d154c3c9d733/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/bc5499b8-2eba-3db4-b3cb-d154c3c9d733/dimension/3> ;
